<p>Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said in a CBS News “60 Minutes” interview aired Sunday that the war with Iran was “not over” because Iran still had enriched uranium that must be removed and enrichment facilities that must be dismantled. Asked how the uranium could be removed, Netanyahu said, “You go in and you take it out”. In a separate interview aired Sunday, President Trump said Iran was “militarily defeated” and said the uranium could be removed “whenever we want.” Netanyahu said Trump had privately expressed a similar desire to “go in”. The statements came as Washington and Tehran were holding indirect talks to end the conflict. Iran’s state news agency said Tehran had sent a response through a Pakistani mediator focused on ending the war and guaranteeing maritime security in the Gulf and the Strait of Hormuz.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/CwNI9gMUmVVRFv4cIje_ZVlX6Cx4j7ASS8SADvHlKdsBbbjQICbHQsKBs1yXdeDI1FfStbj3iQkeShEYIOsVJbWk-2RxV7znrdnAIVe6xxDjVgI95wkyvojuqDr4OuIqXk3gMIOTCVC1fxsjDVNErh0WIhfBxzTZkl70F1Iog1T_8zfXN_9CH5GIvekVTvTESIo2SlBD6nejBYhACuGS5529_GTnt-eKT1L9zA5AUv_UFOWWzR1JV-GnkRdrHOyQ90yvVQO0oj6o' alt='Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said U.S. and Israeli strikes on Iran achieved a lot, but that the conflict would not be resolved until Iran’s nuclear program was dealt with.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Material quantity: The International Atomic Energy Agency has said Iran held about 440 kilograms of uranium enriched to 60%, according to Forum24’s summary of the agency’s figure.</li><li>Wider objectives: Netanyahu listed additional war aims, including halting ballistic missile production and weakening Iran-backed armed groups in the region.</li><li>Agreement route: Netanyahu said the uranium could be taken out with or without a deal with Tehran, and said the United States supported both paths.</li><li>Aid stance: Netanyahu also said Israel should gradually reduce its reliance on U.S. military aid; some coverage cited a possible 10-year path to zero aid.</li></ul><blockquote>There is still work to be done because Iran still possesses capabilities, even though we have significantly reduced them - Benjamin Netanyahu</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Benjamin Netanyahu: Netanyahu said toppling Iran’s government was possible but not guaranteed, according to Israel National News. (<a href='https://www.israelnationalnews.com/news/426867'>Israel National News</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Reports said Trump faced growing domestic pressure to end the war, while some said he favored ending the war before dealing with the uranium issue later. (<a href='https://news.nextapple.com/international/20260511/2B9888BCDE830B7E744D063E764C15D8'>Next Apple</a>, <a href='http://localhost/internacionales/guerra-iran-termino-uranio-irani-debe-retirado-netanyahu-20260510-812808.html'>Localhost</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iran has long said its nuclear program is peaceful and has rejected allegations that it is seeking a nuclear weapon. (<a href='https://www.forum24.cz/iranu-je-nutne-vzit-obohaceny-uran-valka-neskoncila-rekl-netanjahu'>Forum24</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3353068/iran-war-not-over-uranium-must-be-removed-israels-netanyahu-says'>Netanyahu says war ‘not over’ until Iran’s uranium is physically removed</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-war-not-over-enriched-uranium-must-be-removed-israeli-pm-netanyahu'>Iran war ‘not over’, enriched uranium must be removed: Israeli PM Netanyahu</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-war-not-over-uranium-must-be-removed-netanyahu/article70964267.ece'>Iran war ‘not over,’ uranium must be removed: Netanyahu</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/iran-war-not-over-uranium-must-be-removed-netanyahu'>Iran war &#x27;not over,&#x27; uranium must be removed